            the fiber
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t^{-1}(0)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo ^
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\widehat{P_Y X}\to X
            the natural projection (evaluation at
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-,1)
          %p
            In the particular case of the diagonal embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo =
                  %mi M
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi M
                  %mo ×
                  %mi M
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y=M\hookrightarrow M\times M=X
            over a field of characteristic
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by this family of formal groupoids gives back (modulo a convenient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HKR"} HKR
            theorem) exactly Simpson’s non-abelian Hodge structure, that gives a family of formal stacks over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^1
            whose fiber at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
