            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^1:=D^1\coprod_{U(1)}D^1
            as a natural global analytic parameter space for paths. We define
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi L
                    %mi Y
                    %mo †
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^\dagger_Y X:=\{f\in Hom(P^1,X), f(0)\in Y,\; f(\infty)\in Y\}.
          %p
            Remark that up to
            = succeed "-homotopy," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi D
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^1_\mathbb{R}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi L
                    %mi Y
                    %mo †
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∼
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^\dagger_Y X\sim L_Y X.
          %p We must now check that the natural morphism
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
                %em Loops spaces and connections
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3636"}> arXiv:1002.3636
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Damien+Calaque"}> Damien Calaque
                ,
